<section class="narrative" data-narrative aria-labelledby="research-system-title">
  <div class="narrative__grid">
    <div class="narrative__stage-wrap">
      <div class="narrative__stage" data-narrative-stage>
        <span class="eyebrow">Research loop</span>
        <div class="narrative__visual" aria-hidden="true">
          <span class="narrative__orbit" style="--orbit: 0"></span>
          <span class="narrative__orbit" style="--orbit: 1"></span>
          <span class="narrative__orbit" style="--orbit: 2"></span>
          <span class="narrative__core"><span data-narrative-core>Observe</span></span>
        </div>
        <p class="narrative__phase"><span>Current phase</span><strong data-narrative-phase>Observe</strong></p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <ol class="narrative__steps">
      <li class="narrative__step" data-narrative-step data-phase="Observe" data-core="Observe" aria-current="step">
        <span class="narrative__number">01</span>
        <h3 id="research-system-title">Start with the failure, not the feature.</h3>
        <p>Read the task definition, data distribution, and error modes before accepting the paper’s framing or headline metric.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="narrative__step" data-narrative-step data-phase="Decompose" data-core="Map">
        <span class="narrative__number">02</span>
        <h3>Map the actual information flow.</h3>
        <p>Translate named modules into inputs, transformations, supervision, and outputs. The diagram should explain causality—not decorate it.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="narrative__step" data-narrative-step data-phase="Validate" data-core="Test">
        <span class="narrative__number">03</span>
        <h3>Interrogate the evidence.</h3>
        <p>Check splits, pretraining, compute, ablations, metrics, and hidden sources of supervision before comparing numbers.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="narrative__step" data-narrative-step data-phase="Synthesize" data-core="Write">
        <span class="narrative__number">04</span>
        <h3>Write the useful residue.</h3>
        <p>Keep the central idea, the conditions under which it works, the limits that matter, and the next experiment worth running.</p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>
